# Depot DNS Records

Rules for managing DNS records in the depot repository.

<rule>
name: dns_records
description: Standards for adding and managing DNS records in the depot repository
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "infra/dns/dns-.*\\.tf$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "cloudflare_record"

actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      - pattern: "^[^#]"
        message: "License header missing at file start"
      - pattern: "cloudflare_record.*(?!_[a-z0-9_]+)"
        message: "Resource name must follow the pattern DOMAINNAME_RECORDNAME"

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow these conventions when adding DNS records:

      1. File naming:
         - Create/edit files in infra/dns/
         - Name files as dns-TLD-DOMAIN.tf (e.g., dns-com-ponderoos.tf)

      2. Resource naming:
         - Format: "${TLD}_${DOMAIN}_${RECORDNAME}"
         - Example: "com_ponderoos_www" for www.ponderoos.com

      3. Record structure:
         ```hcl
         resource "cloudflare_record" "com_domain_recordname" {
           zone_id = var.com_domain_cloudflare_zone_id
           name    = "subdomain"  # Use "@" for apex
           type    = "A"         # Record type (A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, etc.)
           value   = "target"    # IP or target domain
           proxied = false       # Whether to proxy through Cloudflare
         }
         ```

      4. Common record types:
         - A: IPv4 address records
         - AAAA: IPv6 address records
         - CNAME: Canonical name (alias) records
         - MX: Mail exchange records
         - TXT: Text records (SPF, DKIM, etc.)
         - SRV: Service records

      5. Special considerations:
         - Group related records together (e.g., all email-related records)
         - Add comments for complex configurations
         - Use variables for repeated values
         - Include TTL when needed

      6. After making changes:
         ```bash
         # Review changes interactively
         deploy-dns plan

         # Apply changes and review output
         deploy-dns apply

         # If changes applied successfully (return code 0), commit the changes
         if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
           git add "$FILE"
           git commit -m "feat(dns): update DNS records"
         fi
         ```

examples:
  - input: |
      # Adding a new subdomain record
      resource "cloudflare_record" "com_ponderoos_blog" {
        zone_id = var.com_ponderoos_cloudflare_zone_id
        name    = "blog"
        type    = "A"
        value   = var.com_ponderoos_ipv4
        proxied = false
      }
    output: "Correctly formatted DNS record"

  - input: |
      # Adding email-related records
      resource "cloudflare_record" "com_ponderoos_mx_main" {
        zone_id  = var.com_ponderoos_cloudflare_zone_id
        name     = "@"
        type     = "MX"
        value    = "mail.ponderoos.com"
        priority = 10
      }
    output: "Correctly formatted MX record"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>---
